  },
  "notes": "FP32 contiguous operands. PyTorch 2.12.1 cosine_similarity: NoGrad cloned-norm clamp retains norm derivative below epsilon; zero vector norm derivative zero. Distinct from normalize-dot backward and finite-difference derivative below clamp. Norm squared sums and row derivatives use ascending FP64 reductions, with FP32 norm/normalized/product boundaries matching forward. Each row contribution is stored FP32, then repeated-owner gradients sum ascending rows in FP64 and round once. Both outputs publish atomically; unreferenced owners are zero. No BF16, optimizer or full-head training claim."
